Regenerate two stale pytest-regressions fixtures

Same root cause as ../aiida-orca/regen-stale-fixtures.patch: the already-staged
fixture migration off `aiida.manage.tests.pytest_fixtures` moved this suite
from `core.psql_dos` (PostgreSQL jsonb, which reorders an object's keys by
byte length and then lexicographically) to `core.sqlite_dos` (plain JSON,
which preserves insertion order).  `aiida_siesta/calculations/siesta.py`'s
`for k, v in lua_parameters.get_dict().items():` loop, and the fdf writer's
equivalent walk over the `optical` dict, both just emit whatever order
`get_dict()` hands back — the plugin is unchanged and correct, these two
recorded fixtures are stale.

